			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783639052058,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Now we hit the technical wall. \nHow do we actually code a structure with no rules?\nThink back to how you built a Binary Tree. You created a Node class with exactly two pointers:",
			"rawText": "Now we hit the technical wall. \nHow do we actually code a structure with no rules?\nThink back to how you built a Binary Tree. You created a Node class with exactly two pointers:",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Now we hit the technical wall. \nHow do we actually code a structure with no rules?\nThink back to how you built a Binary Tree. You created a Node class with exactly two pointers:",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
