		{
			"id": "LLAC8dsj",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -390.6998419789644,
			"y": 2958.5090007103418,
			"width": 1088.9986572265625,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b04",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1601217698,
			"version": 594,
			"versionNonce": 637547710,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783639052058,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "But what happens when you try to model a user on a social network?\n- User A has 0 friends.\n- User B has 4 friends.\n- User C has 10,000 friends.\n\nYou cannot write a Java class with 10,000 hardcoded variables (friend1, friend2, ... friend10000).\nPointers worked for Trees because the connections were predictable. In a Graph, the connections are\nentirely unpredictable.",
			"rawText": "But what happens when you try to model a user on a social network?\n- User A has 0 friends.\n- User B has 4 friends.\n- User C has 10,000 friends.\n\nYou cannot write a Java class with 10,000 hardcoded variables (friend1, friend2, ... friend10000). Pointers worked for Trees because the connections were predictable. In a Graph, the connections are entirely unpredictable.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "LUlS4dKw",
			"originalText": "But what happens when you try to model a user on a social network?\n- User A has 0 friends.\n- User B has 4 friends.\n- User C has 10,000 friends.\n\nYou cannot write a Java class with 10,000 hardcoded variables (friend1, friend2, ... friend10000). Pointers worked for Trees because the connections were predictable. In a Graph, the connections are entirely unpredictable.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "nZ4ykLZb",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -407.0121372413796,
			"y": 2356.732694839696,
			"width": 516.999267578125,
			"height": 25,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b05",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 2058272254,
			"version": 370,
			"versionNonce": 2119550654,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783639024643,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "But the real world rarely follows strict rules.",
			"rawText": "But the real world rarely follows strict rules.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "But the real world rarely follows strict rules.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "gSB8Nw9f",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -409.3149647669305,
			"y": 2384.9462022144867,
			"width": 1117.3727747875175,
			"height": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b06",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1490792610,
			"version": 469,
			"versionNonce": 266177570,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783639024643,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "- Look at a map of a city. There is no \"Root\" city that flows downward into other cities. \n  It is a messy web of two-way roads, one-way streets, and roundabout loops.\n- Look at a social network. You follow someone, they follow someone else, and that person follows you\n  back. That creates a circle (a loop).",
			"rawText": "- Look at a map of a city. There is no \"Root\" city that flows downward into other cities. \n  It is a messy web of two-way roads, one-way streets, and roundabout loops.\n- Look at a social network. You follow someone, they follow someone else, and that person follows you \n  back. That creates a circle (a loop).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "- Look at a map of a city. There is no \"Root\" city that flows downward into other cities. \n  It is a messy web of two-way roads, one-way streets, and roundabout loops.\n- Look at a social network. You follow someone, they follow someone else, and that person follows you \n  back. That creates a circle (a loop).",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
