			"text": "An Adjacency Matrix is a contiguous, two-dimensional array used to represent a finite graph. \nFor a graph G = (V, E) with V vertices, the adjacency matrix is a V x V matrix (often denoted as A).",
			"rawText": "An Adjacency Matrix is a contiguous, two-dimensional array used to represent a finite graph. \nFor a graph G = (V, E) with V vertices, the adjacency matrix is a V x V matrix (often denoted as A).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "An Adjacency Matrix is a contiguous, two-dimensional array used to represent a finite graph. \nFor a graph G = (V, E) with V vertices, the adjacency matrix is a V x V matrix (often denoted as A).",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
