			"seed": 1146483710,
			"version": 145,
			"versionNonce": 158880894,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783681545436,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "- Implementation: \n    The graph is represented as a one-dimensional array of size V. \n    Each index i in the array corresponds to a vertex and points to a dynamic list (or Linked List) \n    containing only the adjacent vertices connected to vertex i.\n- Advantages:Optimal Space Complexity: \n    Memory consumption is reduced to O(V + E), scaling proportionally with the actual data rather \n    than the theoretical maximum.\n- Trade-offs:Slower Query Time: \n    Determining if a specific edge exists between vertex i and vertex j requires traversing the list\n    at index i. The time complexity degrades from O(1) to O(deg(i)), where deg(i) is the number of \n    outgoing edges from vertex i.",
			"rawText": "- Implementation: \n    The graph is represented as a one-dimensional array of size V. \n    Each index i in the array corresponds to a vertex and points to a dynamic list (or Linked List) \n    containing only the adjacent vertices connected to vertex i.\n- Advantages:Optimal Space Complexity: \n    Memory consumption is reduced to O(V + E), scaling proportionally with the actual data rather \n    than the theoretical maximum.\n- Trade-offs:Slower Query Time: \n    Determining if a specific edge exists between vertex i and vertex j requires traversing the list \n    at index i. The time complexity degrades from O(1) to O(deg(i)), where deg(i) is the number of \n    outgoing edges from vertex i.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "URCwN1X6",
			"originalText": "- Implementation: \n    The graph is represented as a one-dimensional array of size V. \n    Each index i in the array corresponds to a vertex and points to a dynamic list (or Linked List) \n    containing only the adjacent vertices connected to vertex i.\n- Advantages:Optimal Space Complexity: \n    Memory consumption is reduced to O(V + E), scaling proportionally with the actual data rather \n    than the theoretical maximum.\n- Trade-offs:Slower Query Time: \n    Determining if a specific edge exists between vertex i and vertex j requires traversing the list \n    at index i. The time complexity degrades from O(1) to O(deg(i)), where deg(i) is the number of \n    outgoing edges from vertex i.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
